# vocab.txt — domain vocabulary. check-public.sh refuses to run without it.
#
# COPY THIS TO ~/.config/kontor/vocab.txt AND FILL IT IN. Like deny.txt it
# stays outside every repository: a published list of the KINDS of matter you
# handle describes them nearly as well as the names would.
#
# This is the second line of defence. deny.txt catches the names; this
# catches the subject matter that would identify them even with every name
# removed — a sentence can leak a situation without leaking a person.
#
# One extended-regex alternative per line, matched case-insensitively
# anywhere in the text (not whole-word, unlike deny.txt). Blank lines and
# lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# The shape, with deliberately generic placeholders:
#
#   <matter A term>|<synonym>|<the word a stranger would use>
#   <matter B term>|<synonym>
#   <matter C term>|<abbreviation>
#
# Real entries look like the above with the placeholders replaced by the
# handful of words that would identify each kind of matter on sight. Three to
# six lines is usually enough; this is not a thesaurus.
#
# Write the vocabulary of the matters YOUR branches actually handle. The
# examples above are illustrative and are not what this instance uses.
